FILE: ChangeLog.md
FEATURE: timeline-list-verification
DATE: 2026-10-05

================================================================================
CHANGE 1 — v4.0.0-beta: bullets appended under Added, Fixed and Changed
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
    (no entries for this change; the existing destroy() bullet under Added, which names
    TimeLineList, is left as it was)

NEW_SECTION
    ## Added
    - TimeLineList guide (doc/timeline-list.md) — the attribute contract, the three specificity tiers, centring custom markers, the generated markup, limits, and the error list
    - Runnable TimeLineList example (examples/timelinelist/) — a live playground over every data attribute, three differently-styled lists on one instance, refresh() for lists that arrive later, and the validation errors
    ## Fixed
    - TimeLineList autoBuild() throwing a SyntaxError, and the resize handler throwing on every resize, whenever config.dataAttributes had no smallView entry
    - TimeLineList markers, labels and the label column never appearing: assets/css/timeLineList.css is now loaded by the module instead of never being linked
    - TimeLineList labels drawn off the left edge of the page; …
    - TimeLineList lists picking up another list's styles: …
    - TimeLineList lists added through refresh() getting no styles of their own, …
    - TimeLineList writing "{null}" rules …
    - TimeLineList resize handling re-evaluating every timeline on the page, …
    - TimeLineList refresh() building lists before autoBuild() had run, or after destroy(), …
    - TimeLineList config.dataAttributes accepting non-string attribute names, …
    - TimeLineList config.className accepting a value with a leading dot or spaces, …
    - TimeLineList error messages misspelling "incomplete", "supplied" and "supported"
    ## Changed
    - TimeLineList per-list classes are now vtl<instance>-<n> instead of vtl<n>, and each instance's generated stylesheet has data-id "v<className>-<instance>" instead of "v<className>"
    - TimeLineList autoBuild() called again now builds lists added since the first call, the same as refresh(), instead of doing nothing

REASON
This is the release-facing record of the TimeLineList verification. Added has two bullets (the
guide and the example). Fixed has eleven, one per distinct defect fixed. Changed has two, one for
each renamed generated class or sheet id (a consumer may select on these) and one for the
second-autoBuild() behaviour. Bullets are appended at the end of each section, in the existing
style.
